# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publish
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# private/ is the local-only material: live API keys, a mirror of a device's
# settings/grimoria/ directory, the copyrighted test fixture and everything
# derived from it. It is kept in the tree because that is where the test
# harness needs it, so THIS ENTRY is the only thing keeping it unpublished.
# Never `git add -f` anything under it.
#
# A .gitignore added after a commit removes nothing from history, so this may
# never be committed even once.
private/
backup-fixtures/

# Belt and braces -- the same things by name, in case they are ever recreated
# somewhere other than private/.
*_api_key.txt
settings/grimoria/
*.epub
book_text.txt
prompt.txt
prompt.txt.system
reply*.json
reply*.lua
run_*.log

# Analyses the plugin writes into a book's .sdr sidecar. Real ones are derived
# from real books; none of them belong in the repository.
grimoria_cache*.lua
grimoria_versions.lua
grimoria_notes.lua

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal working notes -- not for a public repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLISHING.md records that keys are pending rotation, that the test fixture
# came from a piracy site, and the whole provenance analysis. Published, it
# hands a reader the project's weak points and reads as an admission.
#
# CLAUDE.md has the same problem in passing (it describes private/ and calls
# the keys known-leaked). It is otherwise the best architecture document here,
# so it is worth sanitising and committing later -- but not as it stands.
PUBLISHING.md
CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output, editor and OS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The self-updater's workspace, created inside the plugin folder at update
# time: staged downloads, and the previous version kept for "Revert last
# update". Both are per-install state, and .update-backup/ in particular is a
# whole second copy of the plugin -- committing either would publish the old
# version alongside the new one.
grimoria.koplugin/.update-staging/
grimoria.koplugin/.update-backup/
grimoria.koplugin/.update-state.json

# The plugin folder is the deliverable; any packaged copy of it is rebuildable.
*.zip
*.zipp
*.stackdump
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode from the test harness
__pycache__/
